{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>That is what I spoke.</b> The thing that I said — that you are spies — is the truth and the correct reading. This is its plain sense. And its midrash: he said to them, 'If you had found him and a great sum of money were demanded of you, would you ransom him?' They said to him, 'Yes.' He said to them, 'And if they say to you they will not return him for any money, what would you do?' They said to him, 'For this we came — to kill or be killed.' He said to them, 'That is what I spoke to you — to kill the people of the city you have come. I divine by my goblet that two of you destroyed a great metropolis of Shechem.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:11.353195800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}